Promote the HQC measurement-integrity repair after end-to-end diagnostics proved the frozen browser bundle was sending /api/event and /api/analyse directly to the AppDeploy API origin instead of through the Cloudflare same-origin proxy. Because of that bypass, the Cloudflare QA guard could not force qa/release-probe/upload-handoff events to isTest=true. Two controlled QA analysis diagnostics demonstrably increased raw genuineAnalyses from 0 to 2, proving pre-fix validation totals were contaminated and must not be treated as authoritative traction. The application itself successfully completed the analysis flow and rendered the Decision Case, so the earlier 0-analysis interpretation was not evidence of a broken analysis engine.

This release updates snapshot rewriting so the AppDeploy browser API origin is replaced with the active Cloudflare public origin. Browser /api/event and /api/analyse traffic therefore flows through the existing Cloudflare Worker proxy, restoring QA-event exclusion without changing the backend, product independence rules, evidence boundaries, custom-domain routing or AppDeploy DNS. A fresh post-integrity baseline must be pinned after production deployment; validation decisions must use deltas from that baseline rather than historical raw totals.

